{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "cbmz_rate_constants",
    "description": "Every rate coefficient of the WRF-Chem CBM-Z gas-phase mechanism (chem_opt = 170, CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP: CBM-Z through KPP, paired with 8-bin MOSAIC), evaluated from the state KPP's Update_RCONST is given. The model CBMZRateConstants exposes RCONST(1:142) of chem/KPP/mechanisms/cbmz_mosaic of WRF v4.8.0 as 142 observeds k_R001..k_R142, each built from the hand-authored rate-law templates of cbmz_ratelaws.esm with that reaction's coefficients bound at the call site, so the mechanism's numbers appear exactly once. It is the first of the three CBM-Z documents: the reaction system (cbmz.esm) references these coefficients by scoped name, and the species tendencies follow from it.\n\nInputs. Temperature, air number density and eleven photolysis frequencies are the ordinary environmental inputs. The ten peroxy-radical concentrations are inputs too, and that is not an accident of this component's boundary: CBM-Z's peroxy-peroxy reactions {127:107}..{136:116} are written pseudo-first-order, so ten of its 142 rate COEFFICIENTS depend on the state. Standalone they are parameters, which is what makes every coefficient assertable pointwise; a consumer that integrates the mechanism drives them from the reaction system's own species.\n\nThe peroxy pool is written as a sum, not as the Fortran's 10x10 double loop. cbmz_mosaic.def's peroxy() builds its cross coefficients from the diagonal by A_ij = 2 sqrt(A_ii A_jj) and B_ij = (B_ii + B_jj)/2, which is exactly A_ij e^(B_ij/T) = 2 g_i g_j with g_i = sqrt(A_ii) e^(B_ii/2T); the diagonal is g_i^2. So the whole matrix collapses to k_i = 2 g_i S - g_i^2 c_i with one pool sum S = sum_j g_j c_j, and the 100 matrix entries never have to be written down. The scheme overrides exactly one pair (CH3O2 <-> RO2) rather than deriving it, and that override enters as a single correction term on k_R127 and k_R129. Measured cost of the rewrite against the Fortran's own loop: 1.1e-15 relative, worst over 16 steps x 59 levels.\n\nSingle-precision literals. WRF's KPP runs in real64, but a Fortran literal written without a _dp or D exponent is default real, so the value the mechanism actually evaluates is its float32 rounding. In CBM-Z that reaches thirteen numbers: the photolysis scalings 0.7, 9.64, 9.04 and 0.025; the .79/.21 branching of O(1D) quenching and the .21 of O(3P) + O2 + M; the 0.667 exponent of OH + CH4; the two constants of RK_CO_HO; and the Aperox diagonal plus the 1.3e-12 CH3O2/RO2 override of peroxy(). Each is bound here as the binary64 value of its float32 rounding, as radm2.esm already does for RADM2, because that is the number the reference evaluates -- transcribing the decimal instead leaves errors of up to 5.1e-8 (FORTRAN_BUGS N101). With them, the transcription reproduces the dumped RCONST to 1.1e-15 relative at every one of the 16 x 59 x 142 dumped coefficients.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "gaschem",
      "wrf-chem",
      "cbmz",
      "kpp",
      "rate-constants"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R. A. and Peters, L. K. (1999), A new lumped structure photochemical mechanism for large-scale applications, J. Geophys. Res., 104, 30387-30415",
        "doi": "10.1029/1999JD900876"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Fast, J. D. et al. (2006), Evolution of ozone, particulates, and aerosol direct radiative forcing in the vicinity of Houston using a fully coupled meteorology-chemistry-aerosol model, J. Geophys. Res., 111, D21305",
        "doi": "10.1029/2005JD006721"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "CBMZRateConstants": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/KPP/mechanisms/cbmz_mosaic: cbmz_mosaic.eqn (142 reactions), cbmz_mosaic.def (#INLINE F90_RATES), and the KPP-generated cbmz_mosaic_Update_Rconst.f90 that assembles RCONST from them."
      },
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./cbmz_ratelaws.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "T": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 298.0,
          "description": "Air temperature (KPP TEMP)."
        },
        "T_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 300.0,
          "description": "Reference temperature of the (T/300)^n forms (the literal 300._dp of cbmz_mosaic.def)."
        },
        "M_air": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "default": 2.4623522626293244e+19,
          "description": "Air number density (KPP C_M = dens2con_a rho, chem_driver.F). Named M_air, not M, because the CBM-Z reaction system has a constant species M."
        },
        "j_o31d": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of O3 + hv -> O(1D) (ph_o31d), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_o31d), index 1 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_o33p": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of O3 + hv -> O(3P) (ph_o33p), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_o33p), index 2 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_no2": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of NO2 + hv -> NO + O(3P) (ph_no2), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_no2), index 3 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_no3o": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of NO3 + hv (ph_no3o), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_no3o), index 5 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_hno2": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of HONO + hv (ph_hno2), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_hno2), index 6 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_hno3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of HNO3 + hv (ph_hno3), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_hno3), index 7 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_hno4": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of HNO4 + hv (ph_hno4), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_hno4), index 8 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_h2o2": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of H2O2 + hv (ph_h2o2), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_h2o2), index 9 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_ch2or": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of HCHO + hv -> 2 HO2 + CO, the radical channel (ph_ch2or), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_ch2or), index 10 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_ch2om": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of HCHO + hv -> CO, the molecular channel (ph_ch2om), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_ch2om), index 11 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "j_n2o5": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Photolysis frequency of N2O5 + hv (ph_n2o5), WRF Registry ph_* in min^-1 divided by 60 (KPP interface jv(Pj_n2o5), index 23 of the 52-long jv vector). Default 0 = night."
        },
        "c_ch3o2": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Concentration of the peroxy radical CH3O2, one of the ten members of CBM-Z's lumped peroxy-peroxy pool. A consumer that integrates the mechanism drives this from the reaction system's own CH3O2; standalone it is a parameter, which is what makes the rate coefficients testable pointwise."
        },
        "c_ethp": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Concentration of the peroxy radical ETHP, one of the ten members of CBM-Z's lumped peroxy-peroxy pool. A consumer that integrates the mechanism drives this from the reaction system's own ETHP; standalone it is a parameter, which is what makes the rate coefficients testable pointwise."
