        {
          "id": "scm_midtrop_afternoon",
          "description": "Mid-troposphere, step 601 level 41 (T = 265.53 K, p = 507.9 hPa, M = 1.3856e19 molec/cm3, j(NO2) = 1.61e-3 /s). Half the surface air density and 43 K colder, which moves every Troe coefficient off its high-pressure limit and the Arrhenius forms far from 300 K.\n\nReference and tolerance. The values are RCONST as WRF-Chem itself computed it, cross-checked bit for bit (Linf = 0 at all 16 dumped steps and all 59 levels) by the standalone real64 replay kernels/cbmz_driver, which calls cbmz_mosaic_Update_RCONST on the dumped TEMP, C_M, C_H2O and jv. WRF is built single precision, but the KPP interface promotes t_phy, rho_phy and the photolysis rates to KIND = dp = real64 before Update_Rconst, so every rate law is evaluated in double there; the dumped inputs are bound here as their exact binary64 values, hence rel 1e-9. Of the 568 assertions across the four regimes 529 are BIT-IDENTICAL to WRF's KPP and the largest residual anywhere is 8.5e-16 (k_R127, surface noon); in this regime it is 3.0e-16 (k_R129). Every one of the 39 inexact assertions is a peroxy-pool coefficient or a Troe/JPL form, i.e. the two places where this document evaluates the same algebra in a different order from the Fortran, and all of them are within four ulp. Dump: data/eqwefic/dumps/chem170_wrf/esm_dump_cbmz_kpp_601.json, level k = 41; the run is described in data/eqwefic/notes/chem170_scm_reference_run.md.",
