        {
          "id": "rich_surface_terpenes_rate_constants",
          "description": "Every CBM-Z rate coefficient at the first chemistry call of the RICH column (step 1, 06 LST surface, T = 306.17 K, M = 2.3565e19 molec/cm3). What this adds over the four idealized regimes is the PEROXY POOL: ten of the 142 coefficients read the ten peroxy radical concentrations, and on the idealized column the isoprene-derived members of that pool (ISOPP, ISOPN, ISOPO2) never rise above 1e-3 molec/cm3, so k_R133..k_R135 are evaluated at a pool the isoprene chemistry contributes nothing to. Here the column starts with 2 ppb of isoprene.\n\nWhich column this is. dumps/chem170_rich is a SECOND reference run, not a recapture of the first: same sounding, location, dates, namelist and binary as the four idealized regimes, with ESM_RICH_IC=1 raising seven initial mixing ratios that WRF-Chem's idealized gas profile leaves at its 1e-11 to 1e-13 ppb floor (TOL 0.50, XYL 0.30, CSL 0.01, ISO 2.00, API 0.50, LIM 0.20 and C2H5OH 1.00 ppb; chem/chemics_init.F, CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP case, WRF fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170). dumps/chem170_wrf is untouched and the four idealized regimes are unchanged. Reference and contract are identical to theirs: RCONST as WRF-Chem computed it, cross-checked bit for bit by the real64 kernels/cbmz_driver, at rel 1e-9. Measured here: 3.7e-16 relative (k_R132). Dump: data/eqwefic/dumps/chem170_rich/esm_dump_cbmz_kpp_1.json, level k = 1; run script data/eqwefic/chem170_rich/run.sh.",
