          "description": "The same, at local noon of the RICH column (step 364, T = 309.11 K, M = 2.3344e19 molec/cm3), six hours into the isoprene chemistry: ISOPP 2.7e8, ISOPO2 6.9e7 and ISOPN 3.1e4 molec/cm3 against the 2.3e-3 they sit at on the idealized column, so the pool sum S and the ten coefficients built from it are exercised with every member contributing.\n\nWhich column this is. dumps/chem170_rich is a SECOND reference run, not a recapture of the first: same sounding, location, dates, namelist and binary as the four idealized regimes, with ESM_RICH_IC=1 raising seven initial mixing ratios that WRF-Chem's idealized gas profile leaves at its 1e-11 to 1e-13 ppb floor (TOL 0.50, XYL 0.30, CSL 0.01, ISO 2.00, API 0.50, LIM 0.20 and C2H5OH 1.00 ppb; chem/chemics_init.F, CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP case, WRF fork branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170). dumps/chem170_wrf is untouched and the four idealized regimes are unchanged. Reference and contract are identical to theirs: RCONST as WRF-Chem computed it, cross-checked bit for bit by the real64 kernels/cbmz_driver, at rel 1e-9. Measured here: 5.7e-16 relative (k_R134). Dump: data/eqwefic/dumps/chem170_rich/esm_dump_cbmz_kpp_364.json, level k = 1; run script data/eqwefic/chem170_rich/run.sh.",
